Manual QA test plan — Music Room
Legend: [] = not yet run, [✓] = passed, [!] = failed (add a note after the line)
Test with at least two accounts (A = free, B = premium, H = host/owner) unless noted.


=====================================================================
users tests: (auth & account)
=====================================================================

registration / email verification:
[✓] register with a new email -> account created, verification email sent
[✓] register with an email already in use -> clear error, no account created
[✓] register with a weak/invalid password -> validation error shown inline
[✓] verify email via the emailed link/code -> account becomes verified, can log in
[✓] try to log in before verifying email -> blocked, routes to the "verify your email" screen with resend (fixed: LoginView was returning `code` list-wrapped — `["email_not_verified"]` — via a raised serializers.ValidationError, which crashed the mobile client's `as String?` cast instead of routing anywhere. LoginSerializer now raises a plain EmailNotVerifiedError that LoginView turns into a flat-string `code` response; api_client.dart's `code` extraction is also now defensive against either shape.)
[✓] resend verification email -> new email arrives, old code/link still works or is invalidated consistently
[] open an expired verification link -> "verification expired" screen, can request a new one
[✓] tap an already-used verification link a second time -> handled gracefully, no crash

login / logout / sessions:
[✓] log in with correct email + password -> lands on Home
[✓] log in with wrong password -> clear error, account not locked out unexpectedly
[✓] log in with an email that doesn't exist -> same generic error (no user enumeration)
[✓] log out -> returns to Welcome screen, protected screens no longer reachable
[] force-quit the app while logged in, reopen -> still logged in (session persisted)
[] let the access token expire while using the app -> silently refreshes via refresh token, no interruption
[] let the refresh token also expire/become invalid -> cleanly signed out to Welcome, no crash loop

Google sign-in / account linking:
[✓] sign up via "Continue with Google" (new account) -> account created and logged in
[] sign in via Google with an email that already has a password account -> linking/merge behavior is correct, no duplicate accounts
[] link a Google account from Settings while already logged in with email/password -> linked, shown in Connected Accounts
[] try to link a Google account already linked to a different Music Room user -> rejected with a clear message
[] unlink a Google account (if supported) -> falls back to password login
[] on the web build: Welcome, Log In, and Register screens each render Google's own rendered "Continue with Google" button (not the app's native button)
[] on the web build: click the rendered Google button on Welcome/Log In -> completes sign-in and lands on Home, without a second click being needed
[] on the web build: click the rendered Google button on Register -> creates/logs into the account the same as mobile's flow
[] on the web build: cancel out of Google's account picker/credential prompt -> returns cleanly to the form, no stuck spinner, no error shown
[] on the web build: link a Google account from Connected Accounts -> rendered button appears (no longer "Available in the mobile app"), linking works and updates the screen
[] on the web build: refresh the page mid-flow (before completing the Google prompt) -> no crash, button re-renders normally
[] compare mobile vs. web Google sign-in for the SAME Google account -> both produce a working session against the same backend user (no duplicate accounts from the two code paths)

password management:
[] "Forgot password" -> request code -> receive code by email
[] enter the correct reset code -> allowed to set a new password
[] enter a wrong/expired reset code -> rejected with a clear error
[] set a new password -> can log in with the new one, old password no longer works
[] change password from Settings while logged in (correct current password) -> succeeds
[] change password with wrong current password -> rejected, no change applied
[] change password to one that fails validation -> rejected inline

account-wide:
[] view Settings -> all sections present (account, subscription, connected accounts, notifications)
[] delete/deactivate account if supported -> confirm irreversible-action warning appears before proceeding


=====================================================================
subscription tests:
=====================================================================

[] a new account starts on the Free plan
[] Subscription screen shows current plan (Free/Premium), and for Free clearly lists what's limited (no playlist editing, 10 suggestions / 20 votes per day)
[] upgrade to Premium via the demo checkout (test card details) -> plan flips to Premium immediately
[] after upgrading, Subscription screen shows "Renews on <date> · N days left" and the countdown is ~30 days
[] premium checkout: submit an invalid/expired test card expiry -> validation error, no charge/upgrade happens
[] premium checkout: leave required fields blank -> inline validation, submit blocked
[] downgrade ("Cancel subscription") -> confirmation dialog appears, explains consequences, before it actually downgrades
[] confirm downgrade -> plan flips back to Free immediately, expiry date is cleared
[] cancel out of the downgrade confirmation dialog -> stays Premium, nothing changes
[] while Premium, edit a playlist you own (public and private) -> allowed
[] downgrade to Free, then try to edit a playlist you previously could edit -> now blocked with an upgrade prompt, but existing changes/songs are untouched
[] while Free, try to edit any playlist (own or invited, public or private) -> blocked everywhere, with a clear upsell message
[] while Free, suggest tracks across TWO different events until you hit 10 total -> the 11th is blocked in either event, message says "per day, across all events" (not per-event)
[] while Free, vote on distinct tracks across TWO different events until you hit 20 total -> the 21st is blocked, same cross-event message
[] retract a vote while at the 20-vote cap -> frees a slot, can immediately vote on a different track
[] as a Premium user, suggest/vote far past 10/20 in a single session -> never blocked
[] the suggestion/vote counters shown on an event screen match the same numbers on a different event's screen (same day) -> proves it's a shared daily count, not per-event


=====================================================================
profile tests:
=====================================================================

[] view your own profile -> all your info displays correctly
[] edit profile: change display name/bio/location/favorite artist/phone -> saves and reflects immediately
[] edit profile: upload a new avatar photo -> updates everywhere it's shown (profile, playlists, events, notifications)
[] edit profile: pick an avatar preset instead of a photo -> replaces the photo
[] edit profile: set birthday -> saves; edit again and clear it -> clears correctly (distinct from leaving it untouched)
[] set music preferences (favorite genres/artists) -> saves and is reflected in recommendations if applicable
[] set field-level visibility (e.g. bio/location public vs. friends-only vs. private) for each field
[] view your profile as yourself vs. preview "as a stranger would see it" (if available) -> visibility rules match
[] view another user's profile who is NOT your friend -> only public fields show
[] view another user's profile who IS your friend -> friends-only fields also show
[] view your own Recent Activity feed -> shows your own actions (playlists, events, friend activity)
[] view another user's Recent Activity -> respects their activity visibility setting
[] search for a user by username -> correct results, no crash on partial/garbage input
[] search for a user that doesn't exist -> clean "no results" state


=====================================================================
    friends tests:
=====================================================================

    [] send a friend request to a stranger -> request appears as "sent" for you, "received" for them
    [] send a friend request to someone who already sent you one -> handled sensibly (auto-accept, or blocked with a message — verify actual behavior)
    [] send a duplicate friend request to the same pending person -> blocked/no-op, not a second row
    [] try to friend-request yourself -> blocked
    [] receive a friend request -> shows up in Notifications with Accept/Decline
    [] accept a friend request -> both users now see each other in Friends list; sender gets a "request accepted" notification
    [] decline a friend request -> request disappears from both sides, no notification of decline sent to requester (verify actual behavior)
    [] cancel a friend request you sent, before it's answered -> disappears from the recipient's pending list too
    [] remove an existing friend -> removed from both friends lists; the other person is notified
    [] after removing a friend, re-send a friend request to them -> works cleanly (no leftover stale state)
    [] view your Friends list -> accurate count and entries
    [] view a friend's profile from the Friends list -> opens correctly


=====================================================================
events tests:
=====================================================================

creating & editing:
[] create a public event with default settings -> appears in Discover for other users
[] create a private event -> does NOT appear in Discover for non-invited users
[] create an event with vote_permission=everyone vs invited_only -> enforced correctly for a non-guest
[] create an event with time restriction enabled (voting window) -> voting blocked outside the window, allowed inside it
[] create an event with location restriction enabled -> voting blocked outside the allowed radius, allowed inside it
[] edit event settings as host (title, description, cover, restrictions) -> saves and reflects for guests
[] try to edit event settings as a non-host -> blocked
[] delete an event as host -> guests see "this event has been deleted"
[] cancel an event as host -> guests see "this event has been canceled", queue/voting disabled

joining & guests:
[] join a public event as a non-host -> becomes a member, can now suggest/vote
[] invite a specific user to a private event -> they get an invite notification
[] invited user accepts the invite -> appears as a member, gains access
[] invited user declines the invite -> access remains denied
[] as host, remove a guest/attendee -> they lose access, notified
[] non-member tries to view a private event -> blocked / access-denied screen
[] non-member requests access to a private event -> request appears for host to decide
[] host approves an access request -> requester gains access, notified
[] host denies an access request -> requester stays blocked, notified
[] requester cancels their own pending access request -> disappears from host's queue

suggesting tracks:
[] search for a track (by title/artist) and by "artist mode" toggle -> correct results for both
[] suggest a track from search results -> appears in the queue at 0 votes
[] suggest a track already in the queue -> rejected as duplicate
[] suggest a track after it already played and left the queue ("revival") -> re-added fresh with 0 votes, credited to you
[] try to suggest without having joined the event -> blocked with a "join to suggest" prompt, joining unblocks it
[] Free user: suggest until hitting the 10/day cross-event cap -> blocked with upgrade prompt (see Subscription section for cross-event proof)
[] Premium user: suggest well past 10 -> never blocked
[] suggest a track with no available preview/stream -> handled with a clear message, not silently broken

voting:
[] vote on a track with fewer than 2 songs in the queue -> blocked (need at least 2)
[] vote on a track -> vote count increments, queue reorders by votes
[] vote on the same track twice -> second attempt rejected as "already voted", not double-counted
[] retract your vote -> count decrements, queue reorders
[] vote when voting is closed (time/location restriction not met, or event closed/canceled) -> blocked with the correct reason
[] Free user: vote until hitting the 20/day cross-event distinct-track cap -> 21st blocked; retracting one frees a slot for a different track
[] Premium user: vote well past 20 distinct tracks -> never blocked
[] as host, is the host exempt from limits? -> confirm host is NOT exempt (subject to the same Free-tier caps)

playback & status:
[] event with nobody suggesting for a while -> auto-transitions through ghost_town/rip_attendance/party_of_nobody statuses; a fresh suggestion revives it to live
[] current song plays and auto-advances to the next queued track by vote order
[] join an event whose track is already mid-playback -> your player syncs to the correct elapsed position, not restarted from 0
[] like an event -> like count increments, "has_liked" reflects for you
[] unlike an event you previously liked -> decrements; unliking one you never liked -> rejected cleanly


=====================================================================
playlists tests:
=====================================================================

creating & basic editing:
[] create a playlist (public, default edit_permission=everyone) -> appears in your list and, if public, others' Discover
[] create a private playlist -> not visible to non-owner/non-collaborator
[] set a cover: uploaded image vs. built-in preset -> setting one clears the other
[] edit playlist title/description/visibility/edit_permission as owner -> saves correctly
[] add a song via search -> appears at the end of the playlist
[] reorder songs (drag or move up/down) -> order persists after refresh
[] remove a song -> disappears, remaining order stays consistent
[] add the same song twice -> rejected as duplicate

premium gating (see Subscription section too):
[] Free owner cannot edit their OWN public playlist -> blocked with upgrade prompt, even though edit_permission=everyone would otherwise allow it
[] Free owner cannot edit their OWN private playlist either -> same block, access alone isn't enough
[] Premium owner can edit both public and private playlists they own
[] Free invited collaborator on edit_permission=invited_only playlist -> blocked by Premium requirement even though invited
[] Premium invited collaborator on edit_permission=invited_only -> can edit
[] downgrade a Premium collaborator to Free mid-session -> loses edit ability immediately on next attempt, prior edits stay intact
[] editing screen shows BOTH banners together when applicable: "upgrade to Premium" AND "request an invite" (invited_only playlist, Free AND not invited)

visibility / access:
[] view a public playlist as a stranger -> can view/play, cannot edit (per edit_permission + subscription rules)
[] view a private playlist as a stranger -> access denied, option to request access (if not owner/collaborator)
[] request access to a private/invited_only playlist -> request appears for owner (and any manager-collaborator) to decide
[] owner approves an access request -> requester becomes a collaborator, gains access
[] owner denies an access request -> requester stays blocked
[] requester cancels their own pending request -> disappears from the decision queue
[] "Join playlist" (self-serve, public playlists only) -> becomes a member; joining alone does NOT grant edit rights
[] "Joined" state toggles correctly and persists after leaving/returning to the screen

collaborators & permissions:
[] owner invites a collaborator -> invited user gets a realtime toast AND it appears in their Notifications list (dismissible, informational only) within 7 days
[] invited collaborator gains access immediately (no accept/decline step) -> can view right away
[] owner removes a collaborator -> they lose access immediately, notified
[] owner sets a collaborator's permissions: can_add_songs / can_reorder_songs / can_manage_collaborators, individually -> each takes effect immediately
[] a collaborator WITHOUT can_manage_collaborators -> cannot invite or remove anyone, and does not see the Invite/Manage button
[] a collaborator WITH can_manage_collaborators -> DOES see the Invite/Manage entry point on the playlist screen, can invite and remove people
[] that same manager-collaborator opens the Collaborators screen -> can see both the collaborator list and pending access requests, and can approve/deny requests
[] that same manager-collaborator tries to change another collaborator's permission switches -> switches are visible but disabled, with a note that only the owner can change permissions
[] owner can change permission switches freely on that same screen
[] mobile Notifications screen and Home bell badge: playlist invites correctly show up and correctly count toward the unread badge

mini player / playback:
[] tap a song preview in a playlist -> mini player appears at the bottom with title, artist, and the playlist name (e.g. "Artist • Playlist Name")
[] tap the header play button -> starts from the first playable song, advances through the playlist
[] tap a currently-playing song again -> stops playback
[] open the full "Now Playing" screen from the mini player -> shows artwork, title, artist, "From <playlist>", scrubber, skip ±10s
[] seek/scrub in Now Playing -> position updates correctly
[] navigate away and back to the app -> playback continues uninterrupted, mini player still reflects the right track
[] tap the mini player body (not a control) -> navigates to that track's playlist
[] start playback from a playlist, then start a different track from another playlist -> mini player switches cleanly, no audio overlap
[] event playback (auto-played queue leader) -> mini player does NOT show (event's own "Now Playing" card is used instead, no duplicate)


=====================================================================
notifications tests:
=====================================================================

[] trigger each notification-producing action at least once: friend request, friend request accepted, friend request cancelled, friend removed, event invite, event guest removed, event RSVP update, event access request/cancelled/decided, playlist invite, playlist collaborator removed, playlist permissions updated, playlist access request/cancelled/decided, subscription... (confirm each shows a realtime toast)
[] each of the above also appears in the persistent "All notifications" history list, not just as a toast
[] unread notifications are visually distinct (bold/accent) from read ones
[] tapping a history notification marks it read, and updates the Home bell badge count down by one
[] tapping a history notification with a playlist_id/event_id navigates to that playlist/event
[] "Mark all read" button (shown only when there are unread items) clears all unread states at once
[] Home screen bell badge count matches the actual number of unread notifications (not a stale/ad-hoc count)
[] pending friend requests and event invites still show as actionable cards (Accept/Decline) above the history list
[] a playlist invite shows as a dismissible informational card (no accept/decline, since access is already granted) for the first 7 days, then only in history
[] pull-to-refresh on the Notifications screen -> reloads everything correctly
[] receive a notification while the app is backgrounded -> OS-level push/toast still appears (if platform supports it)
[] log out and back in as a different user -> only see that user's own notifications, never another user's
